course: dictionary
lesson: 14431
title: Owlets and the little ending -let
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An owlet is a baby owl. Its parents feed it until it is big enough to fly. «The owlet sat in the nest, fluffy and grey, waiting for its mum to bring food.» The clues are nest, waiting and bring food, so an owlet is a young owl.
explain: Look at the ending of the word. The -let at the end means small, so a booklet is a small book and a piglet is a small pig. Owlet follows the same pattern: owl plus -let gives a small owl, which is a young owl.
explain: Some owlets are not babies. Dictionaries also use owlet for a small kind of owl, such as the little owlets of Asia and Africa. When you meet owlet, read the sentence around it to see which meaning fits.
fact: An owlet is a young owl, or a baby owl.
fact: The ending -let means small, as in piglet, booklet and droplet.
fact: Owlets are often fluffy and white or grey, and their parents feed them until they can fly.
fact: «Owlet» can also mean a small kind of owl, such as some owlets of Asia and Africa.
fact: If you know owl and -let, you can work out what owlet means.
exercise: «The owlet waited in the nest until its parents came back with food.» What is an owlet? | A grown-up owl that has lost its nest | A book about owls | A large kind of hawk | *A young owl
exercise: The word owlet ends in -let. What does the ending -let mean? | Very loud | *Small | Very old | Far away
exercise: Find and copy the word that means a baby owl: «The fluffy grey owlet blinked at the moon.» | blinked | fluffy | moon | *owlet
test: «Mum bought a booklet about owls.» In this sentence, what does booklet mean? | A young pig | A large owl | A bird's nest | *A small book
test: «In the story, the owlet has big round eyes and a funny hoot.» Who is the owlet in this story? | *A cute baby owl character | A fast car | A kind of fish | A grown-up teacher
exam: Which is the best meaning of owlet in this sentence: «The owlet hatched from its egg in spring»? | An owl that cannot see | *A young owl that has just hatched | A grown-up owl that lays eggs | A kind of mouse
